d6 6. Re1 O-O 7. Bxc6 bxc6 8. h3 Re8 9. Nbd2 Nd7 10. Nc4 Bb6 11. a4 a5 12. Nxb6 cxb6 13.
d4 Qc7 14. Ra3 {14.Ra3: a rook lift along the third rank. The rook will swing over to the
kingside (Learn: middlegame lesson on rook lifts).} 14... Nf8 15. dxe5 dxe5 16. Nh4 Rd8
17. Qh5 f6 18. Nf5 Be6 19. Rg3 {19.Rg3: the rook arrives, and queen, knight and rook now
all aim at the black king. Same-side castling, attacked with pieces, not pawns.} 19... Ng6
20. h4 Bxf5 21. exf5 Nf4 22. Bxf4 exf4 23. Rc3 c5 24. Re6 Rab8 25. Rc4 Qd7 26. Kh2 Rf8 27.
Rce4 Rb7 28. Qe2 b5 29. b3 bxa4 30. bxa4 Rb4 31. Re7 Qd6 32. Qf3 Rxe4 33. Qxe4 f3+ 34. g3
h5 35. Qb7 {Turning point: Anand's 34...h5. The engine preferred Qd2 (about +1.3). After
the game move it's about +9.7. Carlsen now has the chance to take over. Anand resigned.}
1-0

